course: dictionary
lesson: 10296
title: Many meanings of touching
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Touching is a word with more than one meaning. As a verb, it means putting your hand or another part of your body on something, or being in contact with it: «Stop touching the paint.»
explain: As an adjective, touching means making you feel sad or kind and warm inside: «It was a touching story about a lost dog.» Two things that are touching have no space between them, like two shapes that share an edge.
explain: Touching also matters for your safety. Hugs you want are okay, and you can always say no to touching you do not like. Some touching is never okay, and a secret about touching is never one to keep: tell a trusted adult.
fact: Touching is the -ing form of the verb touch: touch, touches, touched, touching.
fact: As an adjective, «touching» means making you feel sad or kind and warm inside, like «a touching moment».
fact: Two things that are touching have no gap between them.
fact: Your sense of touch uses your skin, and objects touching each other can pass heat from one to the other.
fact: «An adult who asks a child to keep a secret about touching is doing something wrong, and it is never the child's fault.»
fact: A secret about touching, or about someone being hurt, is never one to keep. Telling a trusted adult is the right thing to do.
exercise: «Stop touching the paint.» What does touching mean here? | Making you feel warm inside | Having no space between | Painting it again | *Putting your hand on something
exercise: «It was a touching story about a lost dog.» What does touching mean? | Putting your hand on something | Very loud | *Making you feel sad or kind inside | A rough, bumpy path
exercise: Two shapes are touching. What does that tell you? | They are far apart | They are the same colour | *There is no space between them | They are moving fast
test: «An adult who asks a child to keep a secret about touching is doing something wrong, and it is never the child's fault.» What does this tell you? | The child should feel guilty | The child must keep the secret | Secrets about touching are fine | *It is never the child's fault
test: Which hugs are okay? | Hugs anyone asks for, even when you say no | *Hugs you want | Hugs that make you feel scared | Hugs kept secret from your family
exam: «A touching moment shows love or kindness.» Which meaning of touching is this? | Moving very quickly | Having no space between two things | *Making you feel kind and warm inside | Putting your hand on something
